1. d4 { Notes by Geza Maroczy } 1... f5 2. g3 { The fianchetto
development of the king bishop is the strongest answer against
the Hollandish defence. White has a comfortable game and Black
must be very careful if he will avoid disadvantage. } 2... Nf6 3. Bg2 e6 4. Nh3 d5 5. O-O c6 6. Bf4 Bd6 7. Nd2 O-O 8. Nf3 { Alekhine wanted only a draw to secure the second prize, or he
would surely have tried to complicate the game. } 8... Qc7 9. Bxd6 Qxd6 10. Nf4 b6 11. Ne5 Nbd7 12. Nfd3 Ba6 13. f4 c5 14. c3 Bxd3 15. Qxd3 Rac8 16. e3 Ne4 17. Bxe4 { Makes the draw safe. } 17... fxe4 18. Qb5 1/2-1/2

