19.fxe4 exf4 20.Bxf4 Qe8! 21.Bd6? Bd5! 22.Bxf8 Qxe4+ 23.Kf2
Qf3+ or 23...Qg2+ forcing mate. } 18... Bf7 19. Rg1 Kh8 20. dxc4 dxe4 { ! } 21. fxe4 Bxc4 22. Qg2 Rf7 23. Rd1 Qc7 24. Qc2 Rd8 { ! Avoiding
the trap 24...Bxa2? 25.b3 Qa5 26.Ra1 Bxb3 27.Qxb3 Qxa1+ 28.Kf2
and White wins. } 25. Kf2 Rfd7 26. Qa4 Bd3 27. Qb4 b5 28. Rg4 Be2 { ! } 29. Rxd7 Qxd7 30. Rg1 Bh5 31. Re1 Qd3 32. Qe7 h6 33. Kg1 Kh7 34. Bf2 { This loses quickly. Better is 34.Qc7. } 34... Qh3 { ! } 35. Bd4 Bf3 36. Kf2 Qg2+ 37. Ke3 Bxe4 38. Re2 exd4+ 39. cxd4 Qf3+ 0-1

